.\" Code Editor: the manual page of cedit and xcedit (mdoc; check it with
.\" mandoc -Tlint docs/man/cedit.1).  The full manual: docs/cedit.md.
.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt CEDIT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cedit ,
.Nm xcedit
.Nd text editor for the terminal and for a window
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm cedit
.Op Fl fhnv
.Op Fl g Ar file : Ns Ar line Ns Op : Ns Ar column
.Op Ar file | dir ...
.Nm xcedit
.Op Fl fhnv
.Op Fl g Ar file : Ns Ar line Ns Op : Ns Ar column
.Op Ar file | dir ...
.Nm cedit
.Fl \-lex Ar file
.Op Ar language
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm cedit
is a text editor written in portable C99, with a menu bar, mouse
support and the usual keyboard shortcuts.
It runs in a terminal.
.Nm xcedit
is the same editor in a window of its own (GLFW and OpenGL); it has
the same menus, keys, dialogs and settings, and draws its text with a
built-in font (FantasqueSansMono) or one named in the settings.
.Pp
Each
.Ar file
is opened in a document of its own; one that does not exist is opened
empty and created when it is saved.
With no
.Ar file ,
an empty unnamed document is opened.
A
.Ar dir
is not opened: it becomes the
.Em project folder
.Pq see Sx THE PROJECT .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f , Fl \-foreground
.Nm xcedit
only: keep the terminal until the window closes.
Without it,
.Nm xcedit
gives the terminal back as soon as its window is open and goes on
apart from it.
Use it when the editor is
.Ev EDITOR
for a program that waits for it, such as
.Xr git 1 .
.It Fl g , Fl \-goto Ar file : Ns Ar line Ns Op : Ns Ar column
Open
.Ar file
with the cursor at
.Ar line
and
.Ar column ,
counted from 1.
.It Fl h , Fl \-help
Print the usage and exit.
.It Fl \-lex Ar file Op Ar language
Print each line of
.Ar file
and, under it, the highlighting class of each character, then exit:
.Sq \&.
text,
.Sq K
keyword,
.Sq T
type or function,
.Sq S
string,
.Sq C
comment,
.Sq N
number or constant,
.Sq P
preprocessor,
.Sq D
deleted line.
The language is the one the editor detects, or
.Ar language .
It is meant for writing a language definition.
.It Fl n , Fl \-no-line-numbers
Open the files without line numbers; the lines are then not counted.
.It Fl v , Fl \-version
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl \-
Treat the arguments after it as file names.
.El
.Ss The screen
At the top is the menu bar (File, Edit, View, Help), opened with
.Ic Alt
and the underlined letter or with
.Ic F10 .
Below it are the text area with its line numbers and scrollbars, the
Find bar when it is open, and the status bar.
The status bar shows the language, the line endings (LF or CRLF; a
click switches them), the encoding (a click opens Reopen and Convert),
the indentation (a click changes it), the line and column, OVR in
overtype mode, an asterisk when there are unsaved changes, the project
folder (a click opens Open Project Folder) and the file name (a click
switches documents).
.Pp
In every dialog
.Ic Tab
and
.Ic Shift+Tab
move between its items,
.Ic Enter
does the default action and
.Ic Esc
closes it.
.Ss The mouse
A click places the cursor and a drag selects; a double click selects a
word and a triple click the line;
.Ic Shift Ns +click
extends the selection and
.Ic Alt Ns +click
adds or removes a cursor.
The wheel scrolls, and with
.Ic Shift
scrolls the columns.
The middle button pastes; the right button opens a menu with Cut,
Copy, Paste, Select All and Find.
.Sh KEYS
.Ss Files
.Bl -tag -width "Ctrl+Shift+S" -compact
.It Ic Ctrl+N
New File
.It Ic Ctrl+O
Open File
.It Ic Alt+O
Open Project Folder
.It Ic Alt+P
Open File in Project
.It Ic Ctrl+E
Explorer
.It Ic Ctrl+S
Save
.It Ic Ctrl+Shift+S
Save As
.It Ic Ctrl+W
Close File
.It Ic Ctrl+Q
Exit
.El
.Ss Moving and selecting
.Bl -tag -width "Shift+Alt+Right" -compact
.It Ic Ctrl+Left , Ic Ctrl+Right
one word
.It Ic Home
the first non-blank character, then the start of the line
.It Ic Ctrl+Home , Ic Ctrl+End
the start or the end of the text
.It Ic Ctrl+Up , Ic Ctrl+Down
scroll one line
.It Ic Shift
with a move: extend the selection
.It Ic Ctrl+A
Select All
.It Ic Ctrl+L
select the line (again: the next one too)
.It Ic Shift+Alt+Right
Expand Selection: word, quotes, brackets, line, all
.It Ic Shift+Alt+Left
Shrink Selection
.El
.Ss Editing
.Bl -tag -width "Shift+Alt+Up, Down" -compact
.It Ic Ctrl+Z
Undo
.It Ic Ctrl+Y , Ic Ctrl+Shift+Z
Redo
.It Ic Ctrl+X , Ic Shift+Delete
Cut (without a selection: the line)
.It Ic Ctrl+C , Ic Ctrl+Insert
Copy (without a selection: the line)
.It Ic Ctrl+V , Ic Shift+Insert
Paste
.It Ic Ctrl+Backspace , Ic Ctrl+Delete
delete a word
.It Ic Ctrl+Shift+H , Ic Ctrl+Shift+G
delete to the start, or the end, of the line
.It Ic Alt+Up , Ic Alt+Down
move the lines up or down
.It Ic Tab , Ic Shift+Tab
indent or unindent the selected lines
.It Ic Insert
overtype on or off
.It Ic Ctrl+D
Add Next Occurrence (a cursor at the next match of the selection)
.It Ic Shift+Alt+Up , Down
Add Cursor Above, Below
.It Ic Esc
back to one cursor
.It Ic Ctrl+Space
Complete Word, from the words of the document
.It Ic Alt+\&|
Filter Through Command: the selection through
.Ql sh -c
.It Ic Alt+M , Ic Alt+J
Set Mark, Jump to Mark
.El
.Ss Searching and going places
.Bl -tag -width "Ctrl+Alt+Enter" -compact
.It Ic Ctrl+F
Find
.It Ic Ctrl+R
Replace
.It Ic F3
Find Next
.It Ic Ctrl+Alt+Enter
in the Replace field: Replace All
.It Ic Alt+/
Search in Project
.It Ic Ctrl+G
Go to Line:Column
.It Ic Ctrl+P
Go to File (the documents open)
.It Ic Ctrl+\&]
Go to Matching Bracket, or to the other end of a block
.It Ic Alt+Left
Go Back
.It Ic Alt+Right
Go Forward
.El
.Ss View
.Bl -tag -width "Ctrl++, Ctrl+-" -compact
.It Ic Alt+Z
Word Wrap
.It Ic Alt+N
Line Numbers
.It Ic Alt+R
Relative Line Numbers
.It Ic Ctrl++ , Ic Ctrl+-
.Nm xcedit :
Zoom In, Zoom Out
.It Ic Ctrl+0
.Nm xcedit :
Reset Zoom
.El
.Pp
The View menu also has Show Tabs, Show Indent Guides, Show Line Ends,
Show End of File, Syntax Highlighting, Highlight Current Line and
Highlight Matching Brackets; the Edit menu has Auto Indent and
Backspace Removes a Whole Indent.
.Sh FIND AND REPLACE
The Find bar has the options Match Case, Whole Word and Use Regex,
which are kept in the settings.
The search moves as the text is typed;
.Ic Enter
or
.Ic F3
finds the next match.
In the Replace field
.Ic Enter
replaces the match and finds the next one.
.Pp
The regular expressions are the editor's own:
.Bl -tag -width "{m,} {m,n}" -compact
.It Li \&.
any character but a newline
.It Li [abc] [^a-z]
a character in, or not in, a set
.It Li \ed \ew \es
a digit, a word character, a blank;
.Li \eD \eW \eS
the opposite
.It Li \eb \eB
a word boundary, or not one
.It Li ^ $
the start and the end of a line
.It Li * + \&?
0 or more, 1 or more, 0 or 1
.It Li {m} {m,} {m,n}
m times, at least m, m to n
.It Li *? +? ?? {..}\&?
the same, as few as possible
.It Li \&( \&)
a group, captured (1 to 9)
.It Li \&(?: \&)
a group, not captured
.It Li a|b
either
.El
.Pp
In a replacement
.Li $1
to
.Li $9
.Po or
.Li \e1
to
.Li \e9
.Pc
are the groups and
.Li $0
the whole match.
.Sh OPEN FILE
File > Open File shows a folder (at first the project folder), a
Search field and the folders and files in it.
Typing narrows the list with a fuzzy match;
.Ic Up
and
.Ic Down
choose;
.Ic Enter
goes into a folder
.Pq Pa ..\& No goes up
or opens a file;
.Ic Backspace
with an empty Search, or
.Ic Alt+Up ,
goes up.
Typing
.Ql name/
goes into a folder,
.Ql ~/
home and
.Ql /
to the root.
A name that matches nothing opens a new file of that name.
.Ic Alt+H
.Po
.Ic Ctrl+H
in
.Nm xcedit
.Pc
shows or hides the hidden files.
.Pp
Save As has a File name field instead, with the names that start with
the one typed, and asks before it writes over a file.
.Pp
In the three dialogs (Open File, Save As, Open Project Folder)
.Ic Alt+N
or the New Folder button asks for a name and makes that folder in the
one shown, going into it
.Pq Ic Esc No cancels ;
.Ic Del
on the list, or the Trash button, moves the folder chosen to the Trash
of the desktop (the freedesktop.org Trash, which the file managers show
and restore from), once it is confirmed.
The project folder, the home folder and a folder with a file open in
the editor are not moved.
A save writes a new file and renames it over the old one, keeping its
mode.
.Ss Explorer
File > Explorer
.Pq Ic Ctrl+E
is a file manager: the Folder and Search lines of Open File, the folder
as a tree under them, and a preview of the file under the mouse (or
chosen) at its right.
.Ic Enter
goes into a folder, or opens a file in the editor;
.Ic Right
and
.Ic Left
expand and collapse a folder in the tree;
.Ic Backspace
goes to the folder above;
.Ic Alt+Left
and
.Ic Alt+Right
go back and forward;
.Ic Alt+Home
or the Project Folder button goes back to the project folder;
.Ic Alt+O
makes the folder chosen the project folder (Set as Project Folder);
.Ic Ctrl+X ,
.Ic Ctrl+C
and
.Ic Ctrl+V
cut, copy and paste;
.Ic F2
renames;
.Ic Del
moves to the Trash;
.Ic Alt+N
makes a folder;
.Ic Alt+Enter
shows the properties;
.Ic F5
reads the folders again;
.Ic Alt+C
closes every folder of the tree (Collapse All).
It always opens on the project folder; the project is named, greyed,
under the Project Folder button, as in the status bar.
The bar between the tree and the preview can be dragged with the mouse.
The search looks in all the subfolders of the folder shown.
The right button
.Pq or Ic Shift+F10
opens a menu: Open, Set as Project Folder, New Folder, Cut, Copy, Paste, Copy To, Move To,
Rename, Move to Trash, Collapse All, Properties.
A name is asked for in the Search line (Enter does it, Esc does not).
A document open in the editor follows its file when it is renamed or
moved.
.Sh THE PROJECT
The project folder is the
.Ar dir
given on the command line, else the one chosen with File > Open
Project Folder, else the folder the editor was started in.
It is shown in the status bar, and Open and Save As start there.
The project that Open File in Project and Search in Project look
through is the Git repository the project folder is in, or else the
folder itself.
Hidden files and folders, links to folders, and the files left out by
.Pa .gitignore ,
.Pa .ignore
and
.Pa .git/info/exclude
are not part of it.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Open Project Folder Pq Ic Alt+O
Lists the folders alone.
.Ic Enter
goes into the folder chosen; on
.Ql \&./ (open here)
it makes the folder shown the project.
.Ic Alt+Enter
makes the folder chosen the project without going into it.
.It Open File in Project Pq Ic Alt+P
The files of the project, narrowed by a fuzzy match on their paths, and
a preview of the one chosen.
An upper-case letter makes the case matter; blanks separate words that
must all match.
.It Search in Project Pq Ic Alt+/
Each line of the project that matches a regular expression (or a plain
text), as
.Ar path : Ns Ar line ,
with a preview.
The files are searched on a thread for each core (at most 8), read a
block at a time (never whole), in their own encoding; a binary file is
left at its first zero byte.
A new search cancels the old one.
.El
.Pp
In both lists
.Ic Up , Down , PgUp , PgDn , Ctrl+P
and
.Ic Ctrl+N
choose,
.Ic Enter
opens, the wheel over the preview scrolls it and
.Ic Esc
closes.
No external program is run.
.Sh ENCODINGS
The editor reads and writes UTF-8, UTF-8 with a BOM, UTF-16 LE and BE,
Windows-1252, ISO-8859-1 and ISO-8859-15 itself, and the many others of
its list (UTF-32, UTF-7, the ISO-8859 family, the code pages of Windows,
IBM and the Mac, Shift_JIS, EUC-JP, GB18030, Big5, EUC-KR, ...) from
tables in its sources, with no library; those are never guessed, only
chosen.
When a file is opened its encoding is guessed: a BOM; else UTF-16 from its
zero bytes; else UTF-8 if it is valid UTF-8; else Japanese, Chinese,
Korean or Cyrillic, from the characters its first 64 KB give; else
Windows-1252, or ISO-8859-1 when no byte is in 80h\(en9Fh.
A file read and written back is the same bytes.
The encoding button of the status bar, or File > Encoding, offers
.Cm Reopen with encoding
(the file read again in another encoding) and
.Cm Convert to encoding
(the next save writes it); each opens the list of the encodings,
narrowed by what is typed in
.Cm Find: .
A character that an 8-bit encoding does not have stops the save, and
is selected.
.Sh LARGE FILES
A file of 32 MB or more is mapped, not read, so it opens at once; it is
never written into.
The text is a piece table in a balanced tree, so edits and undo take
O(log n) time.
Lines are counted lazily while the editor is idle; until then the
margin shows the distances to the cursor, dimmed, and the status bar
the progress.
Long lines of any length move and draw quickly.
.Sh SETTINGS
The settings are a JSON file, shared by
.Nm cedit
and
.Nm xcedit ,
opened in the editor by File > Preferences and taken at once when it
is saved.
Turning an option on or off in the menus also writes it.
A file that is not valid JSON is not used; the editor says so, uses
the defaults and keeps the file as
.Pa settings.json.invalid .
.Pp
The true or false options, with their defaults:
.Bl -tag -width "relative_line_numbers" -compact
.It Cm word_wrap
false
.It Cm auto_indent
true
.It Cm show_tabs
false
.It Cm show_line_ends
true
.It Cm show_end_of_file
true
.It Cm line_numbers
true
.It Cm relative_line_numbers
false
.It Cm highlight_current_line
true
.It Cm syntax_highlighting
true
.It Cm match_brackets
true
.It Cm backspace_unindents
true
.It Cm indent_guides
true
.It Cm find_match_case
false
.It Cm find_whole_word
false
.It Cm find_use_regex
false
.It Cm show_hidden_files
false
.It Cm expand_tabs
true: Tab puts in spaces, in a text not indented yet
.El
.Pp
The others:
.Bl -tag -width "ruler_column" -compact
.It Cm tab_width
1 to 8, default 4: the width of a tab, and the indentation of a text
not indented yet (a file keeps its own)
.It Cm ruler_column
0 to 9999, default 0: a ruler after that column (0: none)
.It Cm font_size
0 to 200, default 0:
.Nm xcedit Ns 's
text size in pixels (0: the default)
.It Cm font
a string, default
.Qq :
.Nm xcedit Ns 's
font, a file
.Pq .ttf, .otf, .ttc
or a family name such as
.Qq JetBrains Mono
or
.Qq JetBrains Mono:Bold ,
looked up in the font folders by the editor itself;
.Qq
is the built-in FantasqueSansMono
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "XDG_CONFIG_HOME"
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the settings are, in
.Pa cedit/settings.json ;
.Pa ~/.config
when it is not set.
.It Ev HOME
The home folder:
.Ql ~
in paths and dialogs.
.It Ev XDG_DATA_HOME , Ev XDG_DATA_DIRS
Where
.Nm xcedit
looks for font families, in their
.Pa fonts
folders, with
.Pa ~/.local/share/fonts
and
.Pa ~/.fonts .
.It Ev XCEDIT_KEYS
For tests: keys
.Nm xcedit
types when it starts
.Po
.Ql ~X
is Alt+X,
.Ql ^X
Ctrl+X,
.Ql |
Enter,
.Ql \&!
Esc,
.Ql {x,y}
a click at a cell,
.Ql {x,y>x2,y2}
a drag
.Pc .
.It Ev XCEDIT_SNAPSHOT
For tests: a
.Pa .ppm
file
.Nm xcedit
writes each frame to.
.It Ev XCEDIT_TRACE
For tests: a file
.Nm xcedit
writes each event it gets to.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa ~/.config/cedit/settings.json
the settings
.It Pa ~/.local/share/Trash
the Trash folders are moved to
.Po or
.Ev XDG_DATA_HOME Ns Pa /Trash ;
.Pa .Trash-UID
at the top of another disk
.Pc
.It Pa share/applications/xcedit.desktop
the menu entry of
.Nm xcedit
.It Pa share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/xcedit.svg
its icon
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std cedit xcedit
They fail when the terminal or the window cannot be opened, or when
.Fl \-lex
cannot read its file.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Open a file at line 120, column 5:
.Pp
.Dl $ cedit -g src/main.c:120:5
.Pp
Open the editor with a folder as the project:
.Pp
.Dl $ xcedit ~/projects/site
.Pp
Use the window as the editor of
.Xr git 1 :
.Pp
.Dl $ EDITOR='xcedit -f' git commit
.Pp
See how a file is highlighted:
.Pp
.Dl $ cedit --lex test.lua lua
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr git 1
.Pp
The full manual, in English and Portuguese:
.Pa docs/cedit.md
and
.Pa docs/cedit.pt_BR.md
in the sources; how to write a language:
.Pa docs/LANGUAGES.md .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Leandro Vital
.Sh CAVEATS
In some terminals
.Ic Alt
and a letter must be enabled
.Pq Dq meta sends escape .
There is no language server.
The regular expressions backtrack: one that would take too long on a
very long line skips that line in Search in Project.
